    {
      "id": "numbas-q13336-numbas-52c83c77",
      "title": "Compound interest on savings",
      "imported": {
        "format": "numbas",
        "changes": [
          "PhysLab added a picture (Numbas gave none): the lump sum growing year by year from P to A, years across: compound interest grows by the same fraction every year.",
          "Title shortened from 'Savings compound interest 2' for the practice list.",
          "The rate, asked to 2 decimal places, is marked to the nearest hundredth of a percent rather than to within 0.02 %.",
          "'&euro;' shown as text is now the euro sign €.",
          "The worked steps are rewritten with their formulas set as maths (the original $…$ maths showed as raw text and its nth root lost its n); 'Part (a)' headings are left out."
        ],
        "contributors": [
          "Julie Crowley"
        ],
        "itemUrl": "https://numbas.mathcentre.ac.uk/question/13336/savings-compound-interest-2/"
      },
      "license": {
        "id": "CC BY 4.0",
        "found": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International",
        "holder": "Julie Crowley",
        "source": "https://numbas.mathcentre.ac.uk/question/13336/savings-compound-interest-2/"
      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "number",
          "answer": "P",
          "marks": 1,
          "prompt": "What is the value of P, in euros? ___",
          "tolerance": {
            "kind": "absolute",
            "value": 0.0001
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        {
          "type": "number",
          "answer": "A",
          "marks": 1,
          "prompt": "What is the value of A, in euros? ___",
          "tolerance": {
            "kind": "absolute",
            "value": 0.0001
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        {
          "type": "number",
          "answer": "n",
          "marks": 1,
          "prompt": "What is the value of n? ___",
          "tolerance": {
            "kind": "absolute",
            "value": 0.0001
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        {
          "type": "number",
          "answer": "perc",
          "marks": 3,
          "prompt": "What is the interest rate per annum? Please give your answer as a percentage correct to 2 decimal places. ___%",
          "tolerance": {
            "kind": "absolute",
            "value": 0.005
          },
          "unit": "none"
        }
      ],
      "picture": {
        "kind": "curves",
        "items": [
          {
            "expr": "P * (1 + int) ^ x",
            "label": "money in the account (€)",
            "from": "0",
            "to": "n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "statement": "A lump sum of €\\({P}\\) is deposited into a savings account that pays compound interest for \\({n}\\) years. If no withdrawals are made from the account, then the amount that the lump sum will have grown to is €\\({A}\\).\nThe compound interest formula is:\n\\(\\ A = P(1+i)^n \\)",
      "steps": {
        "items": [
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "The compound interest formula is",
            "tex": "A = P(1+i)^n"
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "P is the sum put in at the start, so here it is €{P}."
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "A is what the sum has grown to after {n} years, so here it is €{A}."
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "n is the number of years the interest is added for, so here it is {n}."
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "For the rate, put these numbers into the formula:",
            "tex": "{A} = {P}(1+i)^{{n}}"
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "Divide both sides by {P}:",
            "tex": "\\frac{{A}}{{P}} = {ratio} = (1+i)^{{n}}"
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "Take the root of index {n} of both sides:",
            "tex": "1 + i = \\sqrt[{n}]{{ratio}} = {intplus}"
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "So i = {int}, and the yearly interest rate is {perc}%."
          }
        ],
        "level": "worked"
      },
      "tags": [
        "number and arithmetic"
      ],
      "variables": [
        {
          "name": "n",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": 2,
            "step": 1,
            "to": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "P",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": 1000,
            "step": 500,
            "to": 6000
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "A",
          "def": {
            "kind": "expr",
            "expr": "round(P * (1 + int) ^ n, 2)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "perc",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": 1.5,
            "step": 0.5,
            "to": 5.5
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "int",
          "def": {
            "kind": "expr",
            "expr": "perc / 100"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "ratio",
          "def": {
            "kind": "expr",
            "expr": "A / P"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "intplus",
          "def": {
            "kind": "expr",
            "expr": "ratio ^ (1 / n)"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "numbas-q20968-numbas-f68f01a8",
      "title": "A definite integral",
      "imported": {
        "format": "numbas",
        "changes": [
          "PhysLab added a picture (Numbas gave none): the curve y = x(2x + 3) with the region under it from x = 0 to x = 2 shaded; its area is shown once the question is answered.",
          "Title shortened from 'Definite Integrals Exam Q6' for the practice list.",
          "Ten variables the question never used are left out.",
          "'Evaluate the integrals' reads 'the integral' (there is one); the answer box takes 34/3 or 11.33, where the original accepted only the exact fraction; worked steps are added."
        ],
        "contributors": [
          "Violeta CIT"
        ],
        "itemUrl": "https://numbas.mathcentre.ac.uk/question/20968/definite-integrals-exam-q6/"
      },
      "license": {
        "id": "CC BY 4.0",
        "found": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International",
        "holder": "Violeta CIT",
        "source": "https://numbas.mathcentre.ac.uk/question/20968/definite-integrals-exam-q6/"
      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "number",
          "answer": "34 / 3",
          "marks": 20,
          "prompt": "\\(\\displaystyle ∫₀² x(2x + 3)\\,dx = \\) ___",
          "tolerance": {
            "kind": "absolute",
            "value": 0.005
          },
          "unit": "none"
        }
      ],
      "picture": {
        "kind": "between",
        "upper": "x * (2 * x + 3)",
        "lower": "0",
        "from": "0",
        "to": "2"
      },
      "statement": "Evaluate the integral. Give your answer as an exact fraction or to 2 decimal places.",
      "steps": {
        "items": [
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "Multiply out the bracket first:",
            "tex": "\\int_0^2 x(2x+3)\\,dx = \\int_0^2 \\left(2x^2+3x\\right)dx"
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "Integrate each term:",
            "tex": "\\left[\\frac{2x^3}{3} + \\frac{3x^2}{2}\\right]_0^2"
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "Put in the top limit and take away the bottom one:",
            "tex": "\\frac{16}{3} + 6 - 0 = \\frac{34}{3}"
          }
        ],
        "level": "worked"
      },
      "tags": [
        "calculus"
      ],
      "variables": []
    },
    {
      "id": "numbas-q21211-numbas-fbc099c6",
      "title": "Calculate distance from a point to a plane",
      "imported": {
        "format": "numbas",
        "changes": [
          "PhysLab added a picture (Numbas gave none): the point P as an arrow from the origin, and the plane's normal n = (a, b, c) drawn from P: the distance is measured along n.",
          "The worked steps' $…$ maths is rewritten as words and a formula line, and 'porjection' is spelt 'projection'.",
          "The point and the plane are written as a textbook writes them (the original showed '10*x+10*y+(-5)*z+2=0' and 'P(3,(-10),1)'): the plane's coefficients are drawn from 2 to 10 and its constant from 1 to 10, which also rules out a = b = c = 0, where there is no plane and the distance divided by zero.",
          "The distance is asked for to 2 decimal places and marked to within 0.005, not within 5 %.",
          "A step puts this question's own numbers into the distance formula.",
          "The plane's equation is shown with the question, so the answer box reads 'Give the distance to 2 decimal places'."
        ],
        "contributors": [
          "Manuel Pérez"
        ],
        "itemUrl": "https://numbas.mathcentre.ac.uk/question/21211/calculate-distance-from-a-point-to-a-plane/"
      },
      "license": {
        "id": "CC BY 4.0",
        "found": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International",
        "holder": "Manuel Pérez",
        "source": "https://numbas.mathcentre.ac.uk/question/21211/calculate-distance-from-a-point-to-a-plane/"
      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "number",
          "answer": "abs(a * px + b * py + c * pz + d) / sqrt(a ^ 2 + b ^ 2 + c ^ 2)",
          "marks": 1,
          "prompt": "Give the distance to 2 decimal places: ___",
          "tolerance": {
            "kind": "absolute",
            "value": 0.005
          },
          "unit": "none"
        }
      ],
      "picture": {
        "kind": "vectors",
        "items": [
          {
            "name": "P",
            "v": [
              "px",
              "py",
              "pz"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "n",
            "v": [
              "a",
              "b",
              "c"
            ],
            "tail": [
              "px",
              "py",
              "pz"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "statement": "Calculate the distance from the point P = ({px}, {py}, {pz}) to the plane π given by\n$$ {a}x + {b}y + {c}z + {d} = 0 $$",
      "steps": {
        "items": [
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "The distance from a point P to the plane Ax + By + Cz + D = 0 is",
            "tex": "d(P,\\pi) = \\dfrac{|Ap_x+Bp_y+Cp_z+D|}{\\sqrt{A^2+B^2+C^2}}"
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "Put in this plane's coefficients and P's coordinates:",
            "tex": "d = \\dfrac{\\left|{a} \\times {px} + {b} \\times {py} + {c} \\times {pz} + {d}\\right|}{\\sqrt{{a}^2 + {b}^2 + {c}^2}}"
          },
          {
            "blank": false,
            "head": "Another way: find where the line through P perpendicular to the plane meets it (the orthogonal projection of P), then the distance from P to that point."
          }
        ],
        "level": "worked"
      },
      "tags": [
        "general maths"
      ],
      "variables": [
        {
          "name": "px",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": -10,
            "step": 1,
            "to": 10
          },
          "description": "x coordinate of point P"
        },
        {
          "name": "py",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": -10,
            "step": 1,
            "to": 10
          },
          "description": "y coordinate of point P"
        },
        {
          "name": "pz",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": -10,
            "step": 1,
            "to": 10
          },
          "description": "z coordinate of point P"
        },
        {
          "name": "a",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": 2,
            "step": 1,
            "to": 10
          },
          "description": "A coefficient of the equation of the plane π."
        },
        {
          "name": "b",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": 2,
            "step": 1,
            "to": 10
          },
          "description": "B coefficient of the equation of plane π."
        },
        {
          "name": "c",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": 2,
            "step": 1,
            "to": 10
          },
          "description": "C coefficient of the equation of plane π."
        },
        {
          "name": "d",
          "def": {
            "kind": "range",
            "from": 1,
            "step": 1,
            "to": 10
          },
          "description": "Intercept term of the equation of plane π."
        }
      ]
    },
