      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "expression",
          "answer": "8 * x + 1",
          "marks": 1,
          "prompt": "In the equation \\(11x - 3x + 1 = 17\\), we can combine the like-terms \\(11x\\) and \\(3x\\) to rewrite the left-hand side as ___. The solution to the equation is then \\(x = \\) ___.",
          "sampleRange": [
            0,
            1
